&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Carvana&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Carvana, we’re changing the way people buy and sell cars. With an ambitious vision and a fundamentally different approach designed to be fun, fast, and fair, Carvana became the fastest-growing automotive retailer in history. We expanded nationally, went public on the New York Stock Exchange, sold our 1 millionth car, and reached the Fortune 500, all in just eight years.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, with 4 million retail customers and counting, Carvana is both the fastest-growing and the most profitable public automotive retailer, and we’re just getting started. We continue to raise the bar for our customers as we tackle the enormous opportunity still ahead in the largest consumer vertical.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working here means being part of a team that embraces change, celebrates creative problem solving, and always strives to be better. At Carvana, you’ll have the opportunity to take on meaningful challenges, learn quickly, and help shape the future of automotive retail. If you’re driven to grow and make an impact as part of a collaborative team, you’ll fit right in. Learn more about what it’s like to work here from the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=93pa9NmlrYc&amp;amp;feature=youtu.be&quot;&gt;people that already do&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel: up to 75% required and must live within a commutable distance to a major airport&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team and position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Director, Field Operations and Strategy is responsible for the performance of new car operations across multiple Inspection Centers (ICs), starting with a core set of sites and expanding to oversee a larger portion of the network. This is a field-based, high-travel role (50-75%) for an experienced operator who combines hands-on production leadership with strong analytical and strategic thinking.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Director will work with their teams, along with partner organizations in Reconditioning, Market Ops, and Logistics, to resolve challenges to meeting IC objectives, while also acting as a strategic thought partner to identify network-wide trends, shaping process and product improvements, and representing the voice of the field in cross-functional planning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is not a fit for someone who wants to operate from a single site or from HQ; it requires someone equally comfortable running a floor and building a framework for senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Leadership&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate effective leadership, setting a positive tone and sense of purpose across each Inspection Center&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Visit the shop floor regularly to maintain detailed awareness of the realities of each IC and a genuine connection to your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure IC management beliefs and behaviors are in line with Carvana&#39;s culture and values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pursue consistent, measurable improvement across your sites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Production Management&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with IC teams to identify, prioritize, and solve problems impacting IQR performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure leadership is executing operating standards including; standardized work, operating rules, 5S, product integrations, and visual management tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor compliance with all health, safety, and loss prevention guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Reconditioning, Market Ops, and Logistics to align production plans, resolve cross-functional bottlenecks, and keep vehicles moving smoothly across the broader supply chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Strategy and Product Partnership&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify patterns and opportunities across sites that point to systemic fixes, and lead continuous improvement efforts across the network to close them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a thought partner to Product Management, translating field realities into clear input on how tools, workflows, and systems should be designed to make field teams more effective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data and field observation to build the case for process, technology, or systems enhancements, and help prioritize which improvements matter most&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit continuous improvement events across the network, ensure adequate resources are available, and hold site teams accountable for results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train and mentor managers on problem-solving and process improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a working knowledge of AI tools to use them to analyze data, prep for reviews, or work through problems faster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and deliver clear, well-reasoned recommendations to senior leadership, including trade-offs and implementation implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;People Management&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with People Operations and IC leadership to build and maintain a pipeline of associates to fill current and future positions and manage churn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a bench of candidates for IC leadership positions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure progression path training and certification processes are consistently executed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide competency-based feedback and hold leaders accountable for providing the same&lt;br&gt;Mentor and develop regional and site leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you should have/know&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree from a top-tier institution preferred, in business, operations management, analytics, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10 or more years of combined operations and strategy experience, including significant experience leading large teams (100+ associates) either as a GM-level operator in automotive or lean manufacturing, or in a comparable operations leadership role at another company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead and develop associates and managers at scale, including building leadership benches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience using data and analysis to drive operating strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some current use of AI tools (e.g., ChatGPT, Claude, Copilot) to support decision-making or productivity in your existing role is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to communicate and influence cross-functionally, including with product and senior leadership, without formal authority over those teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage project deliverables and metrics against aggressive targets and timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to travel 50 to 75% of the time across the network; this is a field-based role with no fixed office location requirement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license with a clean driving record (no DUIs, no more than two moving violations in the last 3 years)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be at least 18 years of age&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to read, write, speak, and understand English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Requires standing for extended periods with frequent stretching, reaching, walking, stooping, pushing, and/or pulling in an environment that may be cold, hot, noisy, or wet, and may have fumes or odors due to vehicle maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Requires use of safety equipment including but not limited to face shield or goggles, non-slip shoes, gloves, mask, and other protective garments and equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to lift up to 30 pounds independently, with lifting required from various levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to walk up to three miles each day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work overtime, weekends, and a variable schedule as necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’ll offer in return&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
