&lt;h1&gt;Automotive Refinish Technician – Buffing &amp;amp; Polishing&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pay range: $21 hourly&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ADESA, is a Carvana owned company, currently operating over 50 locations throughout the US. Our Auto Auctions, some up to 200 acres, provide a wide array of vehicle services including repair &amp;amp; reconditioning, auction remarketing, and many of our sites serve as market hub distribution centers. Our inventory comprises hundreds of thousands of vehicles across North America from retail to commercial, OEM &amp;amp; more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work in a service industry and embrace a “we” versus “I” culture – help others, and they will help you. Our industry is fun, fast-paced, and competitive – and filled with the best people who are passionate about what they do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re excited about the future! As an industry leader, ADESA is poised for a multi-year expansion including huge investments in facilities, massive sales growth, and an ever-increasing inventory of vehicles! We are looking for great people who want to take this journey with us!&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://vimeo.com/652202630/3ae8c047b6%C2%A0&quot;&gt;Get a sneak peek into life at ADESA!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Job Summary&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a skilled and detail-oriented &lt;strong&gt;Automotive Refinish Technician&lt;/strong&gt; specializing in &lt;strong&gt;buffing, polishing, and paint finishing&lt;/strong&gt;. The technician will be responsible for restoring and refining vehicle paint surfaces after refinishing, removing imperfections, and producing a smooth, high-quality finish that meets professional standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Buff and polish freshly painted automotive surfaces to achieve a smooth, high-gloss finish.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Remove paint imperfections such as orange peel, runs, dust nibs, sanding marks, and minor scratches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Perform wet sanding and machine polishing as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use rotary and dual-action polishers safely and effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Select and properly use compounds, polishes, pads, and finishing products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inspect completed work for defects, swirl marks, holograms, and other imperfections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maintain clean and organized work areas and properly care for tools and equipment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Follow all shop safety procedures and manufacturer recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Protect vehicle trim, glass, moldings, and other areas during the refinishing process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work efficiently while maintaining a high standard of quality and attention to detail.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Communicate with painters and other technicians to ensure vehicles are completed according to shop standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Previous experience in automotive detailing, paint correction, refinishing, or buffing preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong knowledge of automotive paint surfaces and polishing techniques.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience using rotary and/or dual-action polishers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent attention to detail.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to identify paint defects and determine the appropriate correction process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to work independently and as part of a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Valid driver&#39;s license preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Willingness to follow safety procedures and maintain a professional work environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Physical Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to stand, bend, kneel, and work around vehicles for extended periods.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to lift and move automotive parts and equipment as required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to work in a body-shop environment where exposure to dust, chemicals, noise, and automotive products may occur.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;1+ year of professional automotive buffing or paint-correction experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working in an auto body or collision repair shop.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowledge of color sanding and paint finishing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience producing show-quality or dealership-quality finishes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Compensation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;$21.00/HR Experience Preferred&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Schedule&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full-time | Schedule 7:00am-3:30pm Subject to change based on business needs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
