&lt;p&gt;We work in a service industry and embrace a “we” versus “I” culture – help others, and they will help you. Our industry is fun, fast-paced, and competitive – and filled with the best people who are passionate about what they do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re excited about the future! As an industry leader, ADESA is poised for a multi-year expansion including huge investments in facilities, massive sales growth, and an ever-increasing inventory of vehicles! We are looking for great people who want to take this journey with us!&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://vimeo.com/652202630/3ae8c047b6&quot;&gt;Get a sneak peek into life at ADESA!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role and Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Mechanic Tech III&amp;nbsp; in our high production mechanic shop, you provide the highest level of experience and expertise in vehicle diagnostics and repair on customer vehicles.&amp;nbsp; Perform major and technically difficult diagnostics, repairs and overhauls or rebuilds, ensuring contractual obligations are met.&amp;nbsp; This position reports to the Mechanic Shop or designated manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A/C, Heater &amp;amp; Refrigeration - Flush system contaminants, evacuate system, add oil and charge with freon.&amp;nbsp; Run OEM performance tests and verify performance, utilize electrical schematics, identify, and correct related problems. Diagnose, and repair all systems and related problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brakes - Diagnose brake problems, replace cylinders and calipers, perform failure analysis of components, Diagnose, and repair all systems and related problems, including set up and use of on car brake lathe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical Charging Systems - Perform full diagnostic, including in-depth analysis and corrections.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clutch - Perform failure analysis for premature or abuse. Diagnose and repair all systems and related problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cooling systems - Diagnose all fan clutch types, diagnose all control systems, replace fan clutches. Diagnose, and repair all systems and related problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Starting/Cranking System - Analyze to identify root cause. Diagnose, and repair all systems and related problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lighting system and Electrical Accessories - Evaluate lighting system configuration and application. Diagnose, isolate, and repair difficult lighting system problems, such as shorted and open circuits. Drive Axles - Inspect housing for leaks, perform diagnostics and major repairs as required. Replace entire lighting harness, lamp assembly and/or control modules on power units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Axles - Inspect housing for leaks, perform diagnostics and major repairs as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transmission and Driveline - Lubricate, perform diagnostics, fluid and filter changes and major repairs or replacement as required on manual and automatic transmissions, differentials, transfer cases and 4x4 or AWD systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All Engines – Check and adjust oil level, identify unusual noises and oil leaks. Diagnose and perform major repairs or services as required including engine replacement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fuel Systems - Diagnose all fuel system malfunctions, adjust fuel system components. Repair and replace fuel system components including injectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical Systems - Perform diagnostics of electrical systems utilizing wiring diagrams and schematics to trace and repair electrical concerns.&amp;nbsp; Use continuity testing, voltage drop, amp draw, short circuit and parasitic draw tests to trace and repair harness issues or identify module failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install/program system modules and perform associated calibrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose Hybrid, EV and ADAS concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preventative Maintenance – Full fault code identification and service interval reset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Steering and Alignment – Diagnose and repair steering.&amp;nbsp; Disassemble, diagnose and repair/replace steering gear boxes and steering racks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Suspension-Chassis and Cab -Diagnose suspension noises and alignment concerns. Maintain, repair, and replace all chassis components, perform failure analysis and substantiate premature failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tire and wheel maintenance - Repair and replace tires, wheels and TPMS components including sensor programming.&amp;nbsp; Properly diagnose and repair the cause of improper wear conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plays a key role in the leadership, development and training of other grade technicians.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and record vehicle information following department processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in overall general shop duties such as cleaning, driving, organizing vehicle parking and staging, etc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide prompt and courteous service to internal and external customers. Maintain a professional appearance and neat work environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practice and promote teamwork at all times.&amp;nbsp; Set a good personal example of attitude and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
