&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Carvana&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Carvana, we sell cars but we aren’t car salesmen. Our promise is simple: we won’t sell a car to a customer that we wouldn’t sell to our own Mom. Period. To make sure our cars are in first-rate condition, we’ve built multiple vehicle Reconditioning Centers around the country, where our cars are inspected, perfected, and photographed before reaching the Carvana website. Using our Carvana Certified 150-point inspection process, we’re able to verify that every vehicle meets our rigorous mechanical and cosmetic standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to provide only the highest quality vehicles to our customers in our mission to deliver a no-hassle, better car buying experience. We are actively looking for passionate and talented individuals who can help us deliver on that promise.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Think you’ve got what it takes to join our team? Keep reading below to see what we’re looking for!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Line Lead Supervisor is a front-line supervisor role, responsible for directly managing and developing a team of hourly associates in an Inspection Center to regularly achieve production targets.&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;Supervisor Reconditioning opportunities include:&amp;nbsp; Automotive, Body/Cosmetics, Inventory, Detail, Photo and Training.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Production Line Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Coordinate and oversee daily operations across multi-stage production lines, ensuring safety, efficiency, and daily output targets are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Cross-Functional Workflow:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage the seamless movement of automotive inventory and materials through various phases of the production cycle, from initial technical assembly to final finishing and quality inspection.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead, train, and mentor a diverse team of technicians, operators, and specialists across multiple workstations, fostering a culture of high performance and accountability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Quality Control &amp;amp; Finishing:&lt;/strong&gt; Enforce rigorous quality assurance standards, ensuring all products meet exact aesthetic, structural, and functional specifications before final documentation and release.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Process Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor production pipelines to identify bottlenecks, optimize material staging, and streamline transitions between different operational zones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3,5,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3,5,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Continuous Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively participate in and champion process improvements, workflow standardizations, and root-cause problem solving on the floor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-path-to-node=&quot;5&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot;&gt;Proven supervisory or lead experience within a high-volume manufacturing, production, or assembly environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;LEAN Manufacturing Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Working knowledge of LEAN principles (e.g., 5S, Kaizen, Six Sigma, Kanban) with a demonstrated ability to identify waste and implement continuous improvement initiatives on the production floor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,2,0&quot;&gt;Experience overseeing diverse operational processes, including mechanical assembly, inventory handling, and aesthetic/finishing stages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What the job requires:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;model-response-message-contentr_549382963645bfe9&quot; class=&quot;markdown markdown-main-panel md-content enable-luminous-fast-follows enable-updated-hr-color force-compact-layout tutor-markdown-rendering&quot;&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;1&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Basic Prerequisites&lt;/strong&gt; You must be at least 18 years old with a High School Diploma or GED, basic computer skills, and a valid driver’s license with a clean record (no DUIs and a maximum of two moving violations in the last three years).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;2&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Physical Demands &amp;amp; Work Environment&lt;/strong&gt; This is a hands-on, physically active role. You will need to independently lift up to 60 pounds and stand for extended periods while frequently walking, stooping, reaching, and pushing or pulling. The production environment can be loud, wet, and subject to extreme temperatures, vehicle fumes, or odors. You will be required to wear standard personal protective equipment, such as non-slip shoes, gloves, and safety eyewear.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Professional Skills &amp;amp; Scheduling&lt;/strong&gt; Expect a fast-paced, high-volume operation. You must be able to multitask, delegate workloads effectively, and resolve complex issues with guidance. Clear, professional communication—both written and verbal—is essential for interacting with your team. Flexibility is required, as you must be available to work variable schedules, including overtime and weekends as needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-path-to-node=&quot;4&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Carvana provides reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities to perform these essential functions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’ll offer in return:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-Time Position with a competitive salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, Dental, and Vision benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K with company match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A multitude of perks including student loan payments, discounts on vehicles, benefits for your pets, and much more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A great wellness program to keep you healthy and happy, both physically and mentally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to opportunities to expand your skillset and share your knowledge with others across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company culture of promotions from within, with a start-up atmosphere allowing for varied and rapid career development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A seat in one of the fastest-growing companies in the country&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
