&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Carvana&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;“We believe CVNA is in the early stages of becoming the next U.S. retail category killer.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;– Stephens Investment Bank, Analyst Report, Sept. 2024&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;“Growing a capital and labor intensive, industrial type asset at a 40% clip is unchartered territory…”&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;– JP Morgan Chase, Analyst Report, Jan 2026&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Building leading-edge technology has been at the core of Carvana&#39;s strategy since our founding, driving us to become the 3rd fastest company in history to organically reach the Fortune 500, following only Amazon and Google. Today, we remain founder-led and as ambitious as ever. In 2024, we emerged as &lt;strong&gt;both&lt;/strong&gt; the fastest-growing and most profitable automotive retailer in the US, thanks to our deep vertical integration across retail, lending, vehicle transportation, wholesale auctions, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our technology teams build:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;End-to-end ecommerce for buying and selling cars, including everything you see on Carvana.com and in our mobile apps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-driven customer support across chat, email, SMS, and voice, as well as a proprietary CRM platform built for efficiency and quality at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;360° vehicle photography and interactive merchandising using cutting-edge computer vision and AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The most sophisticated self-service automotive lending platform in the world; a full fintech stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems and tools behind a nationwide logistics network that has delivered and picked up over 3 million cars via our fully owned and operated fleet, reaching 90% of US driveways.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise-grade systems for operating the largest vehicle reconditioning facilities in the US, with workflow automation covering everything mechanical, electrical, and cosmetic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Early adoption and customization of AI tools to optimize developer efficiency and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And much, much more…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team and position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Product team is at the center of that growth, and we are hiring. We are an AI-first technology organization that moves fast, operates with high ownership, and builds things that matter at scale. If you want to grow not just as a Product Manager but as a leader and business-builder, Carvana is the place for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring Product Managers across several teams in Los Angeles and Phoenix, spanning mid-level and senior roles. While each team has its own focus area, we look for the same foundational qualities across all of them: strong product instincts, a data-driven mindset, an AI-first approach to work, and the drive to own outcomes end to end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on your background and interests, you may be considered for one or more of the following teams:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Nurture&lt;/span&gt;: Lead nurture communications on an AI-first team, guiding customers from early interest through purchase using machine learning, personalization, and experimentation across email, SMS, and push.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Inventory Workforce and Vehicle Management&lt;/span&gt;: Support the design and development of a new collection of AI and Machine Learning vehicle routing and advanced manufacturing solutions. The goal, automate the entire reconditioning process while optimizing for speed, cost and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While responsibilities vary by team, all roles share a common set of expectations:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the product roadmap and lead end-to-end product development informed by customer research, analytics, and business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Engineering, Design, Data Science, Analytics, and business stakeholders to scope, prioritize, and ship high-impact initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own experimentation and measurement, actively interpreting results and translating insights into continuous product improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply AI tools as a core part of how you work, accelerating research, synthesis, prototyping, and day-to-day execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear requirements, project briefs, and documentation to align stakeholders and enable effective engineering execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to size opportunities, evaluate tradeoffs, and make decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take full ownership of your product area and be accountable for the long-term trajectory of key business outcomes such as sales, gross profit, customer satisfaction, and cost per unit sold.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should have/know&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor&#39;s degree in STEM, Economics, Finance, Business, Design, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
