&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Director is responsible for the operational performance of multiple Inspection Centers (ICs).&amp;nbsp; The Associate Director will work with the Inspection Center General Managers and their teams to identify and resolve challenges to meeting IC objectives and production requirements.&amp;nbsp; The Associate Director will also oversee IC teams and ensure solid staffing plans, focus on retention and&amp;nbsp; ensure high associate engagement, a sense of urgency to achieve performance metrics, and a culture that reflects Carvana’s values.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate effective leadership setting a positive tone and a sense of purpose at the Inspection Center&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and develop high performing team within the IC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee plans to ensure the IC will have the capability to meet future demands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure IC management beliefs and behaviors are in line with the Carvana culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Visit the shop floor to maintain detailed awareness of the realities of each IC and a connection to its staff&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pursue consistent, measurable improvement of the IC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lives the Carvana values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Production Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with IC team to identify, prioritize, and solve problems impacting the Inspection Center&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee production planning for the Inspection Centers and ensure purchasing and transportation are aligned with production plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Inspection Center capacity to meet production targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure IC leadership is executing operating standards such as standardized work, operating rules, 5S, product integrations, and visual management tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor IC compliant with all health and safety and loss prevention guidelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;People Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with People Operations and IC leadership to build and maintain a pipeline of associates to fill current and future positions and manage churn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a bench of candidates for IC leadership positions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure progression path training and certification process are consistently executed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model effective teamwork and ensure it’s embraced at all levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide competency-based feedback and ensure leaders throughout the organization are also providing appropriate feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and develop Inspection Center General Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Continuous Improvement - 10%&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit continuous improvement events, ensure adequate resources are available to support events, and hold the team accountable for results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge, participate in and lead continuous improvement efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train and mentor managers on problem-solving and process improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
