&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ADESA, a Carvana-owned company, currently operates in over 50 locations throughout the US. Our auto auctions, some up to 200 acres, provide a wide array of vehicle services, including repair, reconditioning, and auction remarketing, and many of our sites serve as market hub distribution centers. Our inventory comprises hundreds of thousands of vehicles across North America, from retail to commercial, OEM &amp;amp; more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work in a service industry and embrace a “we” versus “I” culture – help others, and they will help you. Our industry is fun, fast-paced, and competitive – and filled with the best people who are passionate about what they do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re excited about the future! As an industry leader, ADESA is poised for a multi-year expansion, including huge investments in facilities, massive sales growth, and an ever-increasing inventory of vehicles! We are looking for great people who want to take this journey with us!&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://vimeo.com/652202630/3ae8c047b6&quot;&gt;Get a sneak peek into life at ADESA!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role and Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Reconditioning Manager&lt;/strong&gt; or other designated leader, you will provide critical administrative support to the mechanical, body, and detail shop operations. This is a non-leadership administrative role that combines clerical functions to ensure maximum production and volume. You are responsible for maintaining accurate documentation, coordinating production flow, and serving as the primary administrative support point for the shop leadership team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Administrative Operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Execute daily shop administrative functions, including entering repair orders, posting vehicle completions, and ensuring data integrity across all internal systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation &amp;amp; Records:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain accurate records for vehicle repairs, reconditioning services, and detail completions. Ensure all customer charges are submitted promptly and accurately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt; Communicate cross-functionally with other departments to prepare for production flow, assist in tracking deadlines, and coordinate upcoming auction requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inventory &amp;amp; Supply Tracking:&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor inventory levels of shop supplies and parts. Assist in ordering and maintaining necessary materials to ensure uninterrupted shop operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting &amp;amp; Compliance Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Run and prepare reports to monitor production volume, inventory status, and shop efficiency for management review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer &amp;amp; Admin Liaison:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a professional point of contact for customer inquiries regarding vehicle status or repair documentation. Coordinate with the front office for billing and reconciliation tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality Assurance Support:&lt;/strong&gt; Verify that all vehicle announcements and reports are accurate for pre-sale and that shop completions are properly recorded in the system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safety &amp;amp; Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure all administrative activities follow company safety protocols and policy guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other Duties:&lt;/strong&gt; Perform any other duties assigned by the designated manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Organizational Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Highly organized with a systematic approach to managing multiple administrative tasks simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Detail-Oriented:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong attention to detail with a focus on data accuracy and process integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent verbal and written communication skills to effectively interact with shop technicians, leadership, and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactive in identifying administrative bottlenecks and informing leadership of potential solutions to improve shop workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to excel in a high-volume, fast-paced auction environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Literacy:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficiency with computer systems, inventory applications, and Microsoft Office (Excel, Word).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; High School diploma or GED required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 1–3 years of administrative experience required; previous auction, mechanical shop, or reconditioning experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong proficiency in data entry and the ability to learn internal shop management and billing software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt; Must be at least 18 years of age with a valid driver’s license that meets requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Driving Ability:&lt;/strong&gt; Able to safely drive a variety of vehicle makes, models, and sizes for occasional lot coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADESA Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Next Customer May Be Your Mom&lt;/strong&gt;: Every customer deserves the same level of care and respect one would give to their own mother.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re All in This Together&lt;/strong&gt;: The company is unified by the shared goal of providing fantastic customer experiences, achieved through mutual trust, respect, and understanding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;There Are No Sidelines&lt;/strong&gt;: Employees are encouraged to be proactive, work hard, and take ownership of what needs to be done in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be Brave&lt;/strong&gt;: Employees should not fear taking risks, pushing themselves outside their comfort zones, or being decisive, even if they stumble along the way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zag Forward&lt;/strong&gt;: The company empowers creative and passionate thinking to find meaningful ways to be different and deliver amazing experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Don’t Be a Richard&lt;/strong&gt;: A simple guiding principle to act appropriately and professionally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay Scrappy&lt;/strong&gt;: This value rejects mediocrity and &quot;good enough,&quot; pushing employees to do more with less to pass savings on to customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADESA Benefits and Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Competitive Pay | Quality Benefits | Holiday and Paid Time Off | Education and Equipment Reimbursement Programs | Matching 401(k) | Career Path Opportunities | And More!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
