&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Specialist in Communications&lt;/strong&gt; at Carvana, you will help uncover, shape, and share stories that demonstrate who we are and where we’re going. You’ll pitch compelling stories, build trusted relationships with journalists, and create content for a growing range of earned and owned media channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is an enthusiastic storyteller with strong news judgment, excellent writing skills, and a talent for making complex information clear and engaging. You’ll collaborate with teams across Carvana to identify stories worth telling, find creative ways to bring them to life, and support high-profile and sensitive communications when needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Carvana, we are industry leaders who take big swings, set ambitious goals, and inspire each other to make values-based and data-driven decisions in everything we do. Our culture is special, camaraderie is strong, and every day, we let our passion and creativity foster innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and develop stories from across the business, working with employees, customers, and cross-functional partners to bring them to life through written, visual, and multimedia content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pitch timely, compelling stories to media outlets and build trusted relationships with journalists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become a subject matter expert on Carvana, the automotive industry, our markets, and the technology shaping the customer experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to media inquiries and support communications during high-profile or sensitive situations with sound judgment and composure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop compelling communications materials, including press releases, media alerts, proactive pitches, talking points, media briefings, and owned-media content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor news, industry developments, and emerging trends to identify opportunities for Carvana to contribute to relevant conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams to translate business results, data, and complex topics into clear, engaging stories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help maintain consistent, accurate, and on-brand messaging across communications channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore new formats and creative approaches for reaching audiences directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other duties as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should know/have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in journalism, public relations, communications, or a related field required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in public relations, communications, journalism, multimedia production, or another related storytelling role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong news judgment and the ability to recognize and develop compelling stories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience pitching stories, working with journalists, or producing content for media audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The judgment and composure to manage sensitive situations and perform well under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in a high-visibility role and collaborating with senior leaders and partners across the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, curious mindset and a willingness to explore unconventional angles and new ways of telling Carvana’s story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI tools to support research, media monitoring, content development, and communications workflows, with strong editorial judgment and attention to accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points if you have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in journalism or a newsroom environment, with strong reporting instincts and an ability to find the story within complex information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multimedia production skills, including experience creating or supporting video, photography, audio, or other digital content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating data, business results, or technical subjects into clear and engaging stories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with public company communications and the considerations involved in communicating financial or other sensitive information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with emerging media formats and new ways brands can reach audiences directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’ll offer in return&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full-Time Salary Position with a competitive salary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Medical, Dental, and Vision benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401K with company match.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A multitude of perks including student loan payments, discounts on vehicles, benefits for your pets, and much more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A great wellness program to keep you healthy and happy both physically and mentally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to opportunities to expand your skillset and share your knowledge with others across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company culture of promotions from within, with a start-up atmosphere allowing for varied and rapid career development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
